WEBVTT

00:28.670 --> 00:30.640
Looks like you slept well.

00:30.640 --> 00:34.430
Yes. These furs are quite warm.

00:40.970 --> 00:42.280
A flea.

00:42.280 --> 00:44.890
Well, you have the finest of fur.

00:44.890 --> 00:46.440
It's the perfect environment for them.

00:47.500 --> 00:51.900
To think you'd notice the greatness 
of this tail! You have a fine eye!

00:53.110 --> 00:55.610
Well, somewhat so.

00:57.570 --> 01:01.240
My white-tipped tail is a source of pride.

01:01.530 --> 01:04.160
As are these pointed ears of mine.

01:04.160 --> 01:08.450
My ears can hear the coming 
of disasters and catch various lies.

01:08.450 --> 01:11.130
They've saved many a friend from danger!

01:12.260 --> 01:18.110
The Wise Wolf Holo of Yoitsu 
is none other than me!

01:20.680 --> 01:23.500
And what does that nose 
you're so proud of tell you?

01:24.410 --> 01:26.370
You should make haste.

01:26.370 --> 01:27.220
What's wrong?

01:28.170 --> 01:29.810
The rain will soon come.

01:36.360 --> 01:40.580
Spice and Wolf

01:40.580 --> 01:41.700
Spice and Wolf

01:41.700 --> 01:47.040
Spice and Wolf

03:05.370 --> 03:09.370
<b>Episode 2
Mischievous Wolf and No Laughing Matter</b>

03:11.370 --> 03:13.490
I thank God for his mercy.

03:13.890 --> 03:15.210
Is this your companion?

03:17.380 --> 03:18.650
This is my wife.

03:18.650 --> 03:21.670
She has some burns on her face 
and always covers up in public.

03:22.090 --> 03:23.490
I see...

03:26.760 --> 03:29.610
Then, I will retire to our room 
after taking care of our wares.

03:47.490 --> 03:50.870
The chilling rain has cooled my burns.

03:53.670 --> 03:55.630
The furs were fine, were they not?

03:55.630 --> 03:58.250
Those furs come from fine martens.

03:58.250 --> 04:00.330
There may be another creature like myself

04:00.330 --> 04:03.770
bringing abundance to the 
mountains where they dwell.

04:03.770 --> 04:04.610
Will they...

04:05.890 --> 04:07.170
Will they fetch a decent price?

04:07.170 --> 04:08.720
That, I do not know.

04:09.110 --> 04:11.880
I am not a fur merchant.

04:11.880 --> 04:12.560
Oh, that's right.

04:12.560 --> 04:14.240
What should I do about that wheat?

04:14.240 --> 04:16.050
What do you mean?

04:16.050 --> 04:20.060
In other words, should I thresh it? 
Or keep it as is?

04:20.060 --> 04:24.150
Well, that is, if you really 
dwell in that wheat.

04:24.150 --> 04:29.540
As long as I am alive, that wheat 
will neither spoil nor wither.

04:29.540 --> 04:37.000
I may disappear if it is eaten, burned, 
or ground down and mixed into the soil,

04:37.330 --> 04:40.100
but threshing and storing it 
shouldn't be a problem.

04:40.100 --> 04:43.700
Then I'll thresh it later 
and store the grains in a bag.

04:44.140 --> 04:45.900
Don't you want to keep it with you?

04:45.900 --> 04:49.390
That would be wonderful. It would be even 
better if I could hang it around my neck.

04:49.390 --> 04:52.490
Is it all right to keep some of the wheat?

04:52.490 --> 04:54.520
I'd like to try selling it to another area.

04:54.520 --> 04:59.370
Many crops only grow well 
in the area they belong.

04:59.370 --> 05:03.940
It would wither quickly. 
It would be a waste to even go.

05:06.280 --> 05:09.160
You still smell bad after 
being drenched in the rain!

05:11.710 --> 05:14.170
I think you are a good-looking man.

05:14.170 --> 05:16.420
You should try to take care of yourself.

05:16.420 --> 05:20.520
I'm at least careful enough 
to not let it affect my work.

05:20.520 --> 05:23.860
Well, I think that beard of yours 
does look good.

05:24.300 --> 05:27.470
Oh? So, you can appreciate this, too?

05:27.470 --> 05:31.810
Though, I prefer it a little longer.

05:32.930 --> 05:33.860
Like this...

05:41.320 --> 05:43.840
We should dry our clothes in the common room.

05:43.840 --> 05:45.900
I believe the room is heated.

05:47.260 --> 05:49.850
There will be others in front of the fire.

05:49.850 --> 05:50.990
Don't let them discover you.

05:50.990 --> 05:53.040
I am the Wise Wolf Holo!

05:53.040 --> 05:55.720
Long ago, I always traveled in this form.

05:55.720 --> 05:57.250
Just leave it to me.

05:57.810 --> 06:00.600
But I would have never thought of it.

06:00.600 --> 06:03.420
Hiding my "burned" face from the public.

06:04.460 --> 06:06.050
What do you think of it?

06:06.050 --> 06:09.040
Such a burn would be part of who I am.

06:09.040 --> 06:12.170
Just like my ears and tail, it would be 
something that belongs to no one but myself.

06:17.630 --> 06:19.060
I see.

06:20.590 --> 06:24.100
I see. So, you come from Yorenz?

06:24.100 --> 06:28.410
Yes, I obtained salt there 
and delivered it to a different village.

06:28.410 --> 06:31.290
They gave me marten pelts in exchange.

06:31.290 --> 06:36.120
Won't it be arduous 
to go back to Yorenz from here?

06:36.120 --> 06:38.130
That's where a merchant's wisdom comes in.

06:38.130 --> 06:39.460
There's no need to go back.

06:39.460 --> 06:41.330
How interesting!

06:41.620 --> 06:46.300
I didn't pay any money when I purchased salt 
at a trading company in Yorenz.

06:46.300 --> 06:48.930
That's because I sold 
an equivalent amount of wheat to them

06:48.930 --> 06:51.510
at a branch from the same 
trading company in a different town.

06:51.810 --> 06:55.980
Becaused I received no money for 
the wheat, I paid nothing for the salt.

06:55.980 --> 07:00.000
In other words, two different sale contracts 
were completed without the exchange of money.

07:00.000 --> 07:03.520
I see. How mysterious!

07:03.970 --> 07:06.380
This is called an exchange rate transaction

07:06.380 --> 07:10.890
and was invented by merchants 
to deal with people in many different areas. {Note: This is a basic form of currency exchange mixed with bartering. You sell your item into a floating currency, then go to a foreign town and use that currency to buy an equivalent amount of something else. However, the prices are not fixed because that foreign currency may be worth more or less in the other towns but should even out in "value" since it should be the same as you physically bringing the wheat there, selling it, and then obtaining salt. We now do it, but with money. We exchange dollars to yen to buy an equivalent amount of the money we worked for to spend in a foreign country.}

07:11.290 --> 07:14.940
I own a vineyard in a town called Perenzzo,

07:14.940 --> 07:18.730
but I've never made a payment 
in such an unusual way.

07:19.120 --> 07:21.370
Do you think I should know about such a system?

07:21.370 --> 07:23.010
No, it's unnecessary.

07:23.010 --> 07:25.340
As a lord who owns a vineyard,

07:25.340 --> 07:28.520
you just need to make sure merchants don't take 
advantage of you during price negotiations.

07:28.520 --> 07:31.530
That becomes a dispute every year.

07:32.420 --> 07:34.390
You said your name was Lawrence?

07:35.200 --> 07:40.230
If you ever visit Perenzzo, 
please stop by my house.

07:40.230 --> 07:41.960
You will be most welcome.

07:41.960 --> 07:43.810
Yes, I would love to.

07:44.140 --> 07:47.180
Well, it seems my wife is a bit tired...

07:48.420 --> 07:50.010
We will excuse ourselves for the night.

07:50.780 --> 07:55.350
Well, may God bring us together once again.

08:01.090 --> 08:04.340
Mister, you're pretty good.

08:04.340 --> 08:06.320
I'm just an ordinary merchant.

08:06.320 --> 08:10.500
No, no! I was aiming 
for that couple myself,

08:10.500 --> 08:12.800
but I couldn't quite seize an opportunity.

08:12.800 --> 08:15.550
But you were able to do it so easily!

08:15.900 --> 08:19.780
When I was starting out, other 
merchants looked like monsters to me.

08:20.190 --> 08:23.690
Even now, more than half are still monsters. 
You just have to try your best.

08:23.690 --> 08:26.590
Well, that makes me feel a little better.

08:28.540 --> 08:31.600
My name is Zheren.

08:31.600 --> 08:33.820
I'm a rookie merchant.

08:37.820 --> 08:39.050
I'm Lawrence.

08:40.730 --> 08:43.510
Is this your companion?

08:45.950 --> 08:47.580
This is my wife, Holo.

08:48.590 --> 08:50.460
You're traveling together with your wife?

08:50.460 --> 08:55.470
You must really treasure her, 
considering how much you cover her up.

08:55.470 --> 08:58.050
I'm sure God brought us together 
for this encounter.

08:58.050 --> 09:01.470
Would you let me take a look?

09:01.470 --> 09:02.160
Well...

09:02.160 --> 09:05.200
A journey is the most enjoyable 
before one sets out.

09:05.200 --> 09:08.460
The most frightening part of a dog is its bark.

09:08.460 --> 09:12.440
And women look the most beautiful 
when viewed from behind.

09:12.440 --> 09:16.660
Uncovering a hood so casually 
can easily dispel the fantasy.

09:16.660 --> 09:19.740
I could never do something like that to you.

09:21.370 --> 09:23.980
Wow, your wife is really something.

09:23.980 --> 09:26.890
It takes everything I have just to avoid 
being completely under her thumb.

09:28.170 --> 09:31.970
God must have guided me to the two of you.

09:31.970 --> 09:33.590
How about it, mister?

09:33.590 --> 09:37.700
Would you listen to what I have to say?

09:44.750 --> 09:46.520
It smells so good!

09:46.850 --> 09:49.480
Goat cheese over boiled potatoes?!

09:50.140 --> 09:51.220
Hold on.

09:54.160 --> 09:55.400
Wheat?

09:55.400 --> 09:58.990
I tied a leather string around it 
so you can hang it around your neck.

09:59.420 --> 10:01.490
Yes, thank you.

10:04.230 --> 10:05.530
However...

10:07.540 --> 10:08.960
This is currently more important!

10:08.960 --> 10:10.250
Hold on!

10:10.620 --> 10:11.960
Again?!

10:12.490 --> 10:14.350
The leather string and the bag of wheat.

10:14.780 --> 10:16.980
I even got goat cheese 
on the potatoes as a treat.

10:16.980 --> 10:19.300
I had to donate a lot of money for all of it.

10:19.300 --> 10:21.970
On top of that, my best clothes!

10:21.970 --> 10:24.010
You'll have to pay me back for all of it!

10:26.580 --> 10:28.170
Is that all?

10:28.170 --> 10:29.010
Yes.

10:31.910 --> 10:35.350
Vegetables grown by humans 
taste better than foraged nuts.

10:36.030 --> 10:39.570
I love the idea of cooking them with heat.

10:49.040 --> 10:51.860
Human throats are so narrow.

10:51.860 --> 10:53.300
How inconvenient!

10:53.300 --> 10:55.340
Well, wolves eat their food without chewing.

10:56.900 --> 10:58.340
Well, of course.

10:59.470 --> 11:01.090
We have no cheek space.

11:01.420 --> 11:03.620
I cannot take my time to chew.

11:05.060 --> 11:08.940
However, I have choked on potatoes once before.

11:08.940 --> 11:10.990
They may not be compatible with me.

11:18.580 --> 11:22.770
Come to think of it, didn't you say 
you can tell when people are lying?

11:24.740 --> 11:26.240
Yes, more or less.

11:26.550 --> 11:27.770
To what extent?

11:31.140 --> 11:33.780
Well, to the point that I could tell

11:33.780 --> 11:37.340
you praised my tail even though 
you didn't genuinely think so.

11:38.670 --> 11:41.520
I am not right all the time.

11:41.520 --> 11:46.210
Well, it's up to you to whether 
you believe me or not.

11:47.640 --> 11:49.400
Then, let me ask you this.

11:49.400 --> 11:51.730
What do you think of that kid?

11:51.730 --> 11:53.140
Kid?

11:53.140 --> 11:56.100
The one who talked to us 
in front of the fireplace.

11:56.100 --> 11:57.190
Oh!

11:58.180 --> 12:00.940
You are both kids in my eyes.

12:03.110 --> 12:06.240
Though you are just a bit more mature.

12:07.860 --> 12:10.230
What that kid told us, huh?

12:12.540 --> 12:14.180
Actually, Mister,

12:14.180 --> 12:18.380
it's rumored that a certain silver coin 
that is currently being circulated

12:18.380 --> 12:21.260
will soon be replaced with coins 
that have a higher percentage of silver.

12:21.560 --> 12:22.300
Oh?

12:22.300 --> 12:28.470
The new silver coin is still 
worth the same as the old silver coin,

12:28.470 --> 12:34.090
but the new coins will be worth more when 
exchanged for the currency of other countries.

12:34.090 --> 12:35.380
In other words...

12:34.090 --> 12:35.380
In other words...

12:36.570 --> 12:39.330
If we collect a large amount 
of the current silver coins

12:39.330 --> 12:42.730
and exchange them with the new coins 
when they become available,

12:42.730 --> 12:45.740
we can make a huge profit from the difference.

12:45.740 --> 12:48.580
As expected! You're so quick to catch on!

12:48.580 --> 12:54.460
What do you say? 
I can tell you which silver coin it is.

12:54.460 --> 12:58.460
In exchange, how about giving me a share 
once you make a big profit?

13:05.460 --> 13:08.430
I believe that kid is lying.

13:08.850 --> 13:12.150
Though I don't know exactly 
what part he may be lying about.

13:12.730 --> 13:13.640
I see.

13:14.140 --> 13:18.610
Currency speculation itself 
isn't that rare, but...

13:18.610 --> 13:21.490
You don't know why he'd lie about such a thing.

13:21.490 --> 13:22.320
Am I right?

13:24.220 --> 13:30.930
When one lies, the reason for the lie 
is more important than the lie itself.

13:32.380 --> 13:33.540
You're right.

13:34.250 --> 13:37.030
It took me many years to realize that.

13:39.630 --> 13:41.680
There is no need 
to be bothered by such a thing.

13:41.680 --> 13:45.340
After all, you are still a kid in my eyes.

13:48.380 --> 13:53.020
What would you have done if I was not here?

13:53.020 --> 13:54.430
If I was alone?

13:58.130 --> 14:00.660
I'd put aside whether 
the information was true or false.

14:01.170 --> 14:04.110
And I'd act like I was 
interested in Zheren's offer.

14:04.110 --> 14:06.110
And why would you do that?

14:06.110 --> 14:09.490
If it were true, I'd make a profit.

14:09.490 --> 14:13.020
If it were false, that means 
someone is plotting something.

14:13.020 --> 14:18.590
If I investigate it carefully, it'll usually 
connect to some kind of moneymaking scheme.

14:19.830 --> 14:23.880
Now that I have told you it was a lie?

14:24.200 --> 14:25.170
Well...

14:27.820 --> 14:31.340
There was nothing to 
hesitate about from the start.

14:31.340 --> 14:34.640
You are going to act like 
you are interested, either way.

14:37.270 --> 14:39.700
It seems these extra potatoes are mine.

14:44.940 --> 14:47.250
I am the Wise Wolf Holo.

14:47.250 --> 14:49.940
How many of your lifetimes 
do you think I have lived?

15:38.590 --> 15:40.660
May my dear husband...

15:40.660 --> 15:43.210
have more pluck!

15:49.880 --> 15:51.040
Goodness.

15:51.040 --> 15:52.890
What were you doing so early in the morning?

15:52.890 --> 15:57.010
I woke up early, 
so I listened to their preaching.

15:57.010 --> 15:59.060
Something like that interested you?

15:59.060 --> 16:01.740
It is interesting to listen to on occasion.

16:03.700 --> 16:07.620
At any rate, it seems they have 
grown quite important.

16:07.620 --> 16:09.900
The Church has always been important.

16:10.370 --> 16:11.980
Not so.

16:11.980 --> 16:16.020
It was not as important when 
I first arrived here from the north.

16:16.490 --> 16:17.740
At the very least,

16:17.740 --> 16:22.060
they did not say exaggerated things 
like "the one true God created the world"

16:22.060 --> 16:24.830
and that we are merely "borrowing" it.

16:25.460 --> 16:28.930
Nature cannot be created by someone.

16:28.930 --> 16:34.550
It made me wonder when the Church 
began to perform such comedies.

16:36.990 --> 16:39.630
This must also be a change of the times.

16:40.330 --> 16:42.890
It seems the world has changed a lot.

16:45.270 --> 16:47.250
Have you changed?

16:51.330 --> 16:54.030
Then I'm sure your hometown 
hasn't changed, either.

16:59.250 --> 17:02.750
Being comforted by you 
is a disgrace to a Wise Wolf.

17:10.910 --> 17:11.970
Hey!

17:12.590 --> 17:15.890
Come quickly! What are you doing?!

17:23.570 --> 17:27.620
Is that so?! You're in?!

17:27.620 --> 17:29.610
However, I can't pay upfront.

17:29.990 --> 17:33.360
I have no funds until 
I exchange my furs for money.

17:33.360 --> 17:39.870
Then, let's meet up in the port town 
of Pazzio and draw up an official contract!

17:40.250 --> 17:43.900
Once you arrive in Pazzio, 
please stop by a bar called Yorrend.

17:43.900 --> 17:46.040
You'll be able to contact me there.

17:46.040 --> 17:47.330
Yorrend?

17:47.330 --> 17:49.580
Yes, then I'll head out first.

17:49.930 --> 17:52.840
Safe travels, Mister!

17:53.300 --> 17:55.130
Are we not traveling together?

17:55.130 --> 17:56.960
The roads are muddy.

17:56.960 --> 17:59.390
Walking will be far faster 
than traveling by carriage.

17:59.390 --> 18:02.450
There's no need to force him 
to follow a slow carriage.

18:03.100 --> 18:06.660
True. Merchants are stingy with their time.

18:07.770 --> 18:10.230
Time is money.

18:11.430 --> 18:13.110
What an interesting phrase.

18:13.590 --> 18:15.860
Time is money, huh?

18:16.380 --> 18:21.070
The farmers you've watched over for hundreds 
of years are also particular about time.

18:21.070 --> 18:23.200
What are you paying attention to?

18:23.620 --> 18:25.680
They are not particular about time.

18:25.680 --> 18:27.620
They are particular about sensing things.

18:29.510 --> 18:30.750
I don't understand.

18:31.140 --> 18:32.210
For instance...

18:32.690 --> 18:35.380
They awaken when they sense daybreak

18:35.380 --> 18:37.670
and pull weeds when they sense the afternoon.

18:38.270 --> 18:40.650
They rejoice the budding sprouts 
as they sense spring,

18:40.650 --> 18:43.260
enjoy the growth of the crops 
as they sense summer,

18:43.750 --> 18:46.250
celebrate the harvest as they sense autumn,

18:46.250 --> 18:49.100
and they wait for spring as they sense winter.

18:49.100 --> 18:51.800
They do not care about time.

18:51.800 --> 18:53.230
It is the same for me.

18:53.830 --> 18:57.690
Your mind is quick, but you lack experience.

19:04.230 --> 19:09.440
To put it another way, you will become 
well-established as you age.

19:09.440 --> 19:11.460
How many hundreds of years 
are you talking about?

19:13.470 --> 19:16.040
Your wits are indeed sharp.

19:16.040 --> 19:19.920
Perhaps yours are just too old, 
so they're starting to break down?

19:21.620 --> 19:25.470
Do you know why we wolves attack humans?

19:26.660 --> 19:27.390
No.

19:28.190 --> 19:34.110
It is because we wish to eat 
their heads and gain their power.

19:35.570 --> 19:38.220
You are still a mere chick in my eyes.

19:38.220 --> 19:40.530
You are no match for me.

19:43.520 --> 19:47.020
Have you ever been attacked by a wolf?

19:47.020 --> 19:47.700
I have.

19:48.170 --> 19:49.260
About eight times.

19:52.410 --> 19:53.900
Formidable, were they not?

19:53.900 --> 19:54.670
Yes.

19:55.740 --> 19:59.530
I've made it through bands 
of wild dogs, but wolves...

20:01.510 --> 20:02.520
are really formidable.

20:03.180 --> 20:07.680
That's because they have eaten 
many humans and gained their—

20:07.680 --> 20:08.720
Stop!

20:10.420 --> 20:12.620
I apologize for saying 
your brain is breaking down.

20:13.330 --> 20:14.170
So,

20:15.270 --> 20:16.520
please stop.

20:32.030 --> 20:33.340
My apologies...

20:46.290 --> 20:47.640
Are you angry?

20:47.640 --> 20:48.870
I am.

20:49.450 --> 20:51.680
So, don't ever joke about 
something like that again.

21:03.790 --> 21:06.290
Let's sleep around that area tonight.

21:07.540 --> 21:12.910
Wolves have only lived in the forest 
while dogs have lived beside humans before.

21:14.110 --> 21:17.740
That's the difference between 
the difficulty of wolves and dogs.

21:18.170 --> 21:21.380
Wolves have only been hunted by humans.

21:21.820 --> 21:24.010
Humans are a source of fear for us.

21:24.010 --> 21:25.490
That's why we think about

21:25.940 --> 21:29.770
how to best humans when they enter our forests.

21:33.940 --> 21:35.230
Does that mean that you've also...

21:35.770 --> 21:39.980
There are things that even I refuse to answer.

21:42.180 --> 21:43.260
I'm sorry.

21:43.990 --> 21:45.940
Now, we are even.

22:02.590 --> 22:07.050
You and I have lived 
in completely different worlds.

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Episode 3

23:45.020 --> 23:50.030
Port Town and Sweet Temptation

23:45.820 --> 23:49.220
Next Episode: "Port Town and Sweet Temptation"
